Got a good way into this PR (all the `dispatcher.ts` changes) when I realized we are already attempting to be case insensitive on paths. Check out `module-tree.ts`:

```
  private buildMatch(
    directory: Directory,
    segment: string,
    pathVariables: { [key: string]: string },
    matchedPath: string,
  ) {
    const match =
      directory.files[segment.toLowerCase()] ??
      Object.values(directory.files).find((file) => file.isWildcard);
```
In there we match `directory.files` on the lower case of `segment`. This appears to me that part of the codebase cares about case and part does not. I noticed this because of the tests I was adding to `dispatcher`. It was still passing on invalid-case paths because the `module-tree` matcher was finding the paths.

Thoughts? Do we just make it case-insensitive across the board without a config option or do we add the config option and update `module-tree` to care about case?

